1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,830
This video shows you how to find what's wrong in your fleet, and why.

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,969
Status lists every worker, by worker group.

3
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:14,030
Both workers are online, and run the same commit.

4
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:17,345
Rows in and out shows the whole fleet's flow.

5
00:00:17,345 --> 00:00:20,392
Above the line are rows read from sources.

6
00:00:20,392 --> 00:00:23,821
Below it are rows sent to destinations.

7
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,680
Now something breaks.

8
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:30,710
A red banner lists the active issues, and both workers need attention.

9
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:31,730
Open Issues.

10
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:37,870
Destination unreachable names tutorial-out, on both workers in the group.

11
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:41,093
The message says what to check: that the broker is up,

12
00:00:41,093 --> 00:00:45,470
that the worker can reach it, and that its credentials are still valid.

13
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,887
Each worker also logged the error.

14
00:00:47,887 --> 00:00:53,070
Issues lists a worker's logged errors and warnings as Logged a warning.

15
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:54,920
Map traces the flow.

16
00:00:54,920 --> 00:01:00,430
tutorial-in still reads, but tutorial-out delivers nothing.

17
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:02,364
The source's lag grows.

18
00:01:02,364 --> 00:01:06,990
Its rows wait in Kafka until the destination recovers.

19
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:08,895
Logs give the detail.

20
00:01:08,895 --> 00:01:11,703
Choose error, and Search.

21
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:20,333
Each worker tried to connect to kafka-out.example.com,

22
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:24,011
on port 9094, and the connection was refused.

23
00:01:24,011 --> 00:01:27,190
Here, that means the broker is down.

24
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:27,945
Add warn.

25
00:01:27,945 --> 00:01:30,061
The destination is stalled.

26
00:01:30,061 --> 00:01:36,145
Its rows are held and sent again once it recovers, so nothing is lost.

27
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:42,639
Once the broker is back, Destination unreachable clears, and the lag drains.

28
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:49,511
A logged warning fades five minutes after the worker last logged it.

29
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:53,541
A worker that stops answering shows as Silent.

30
00:01:53,541 --> 00:01:55,910
Its last seen time turns red.

31
00:01:55,960 --> 00:02:00,350
Its partitions move to the other worker, so rows keep flowing.

32
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,522
Check on learning.

33
00:02:02,722 --> 00:02:05,194
A destination stops taking rows.

34
00:02:05,194 --> 00:02:09,038
Where do you see which one it is, and why?

35
00:02:13,438 --> 00:02:14,263
On Issues.

36
00:02:14,263 --> 00:02:18,220
It names the destination and says what to check.

37
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:20,552
Logs give the detail.

38
00:02:21,452 --> 00:02:26,319
Next, send your fleet's logs and metrics to your own platform.
